# Concrete witnesses for the Fi23 kernel stabilizer chain

The proposed chain uses the fixed letters 1, 13, 27, 40, 46, 63, 66, 78,
86, 108 (zero based). The seven intermediate permutations were produced by
GAP after stabilizing the first three letters. These are definitions only:
no assertion that this group is the actual stabilizer is made here.

`KernelData/Generate.g` and `KernelData/Encode.py` reproduce these witnesses
from the retained ATLAS F23G1-p31671B0 sources. As in `CycleEncoding`, each
right-action permutation is inverted to obtain a left-action permutation.
The two mathematical obligations are containment of the three-point stabilizer
in this generated group and rigidity of its seven-point stabilizer. Both
require Lean proofs; GAP's stabilizer computation is not trusted.

Source application: GLS volume 3, Table 5.3u and the Fischer paragraph at
line 1042 of `refs/KGroup/GLS3/Chapter5(sec3-).tex`.
